If you're diagnosed with bruxism, there are treatment options beyond wearing a mouth guard at night. Your dentist or doctor might recommend stress-reducing techniques, such as meditation or yoga, to help manage tension that could be contributing to teeth grinding. They might also suggest physical therapy to relax your jaw muscles or prescribe muscle relaxants in some cases. Additionally, making lifestyle changes like improving your sleep posture, avoiding caffeine and alcohol before bedtime, and engaging in regular exercise can help alleviate bruxism symptoms.

It's essential to consult with a healthcare professional to determine the best course of action for your specific situation. They can help you weigh the pros and cons of different treatment options and develop a personalized plan to address your headaches and potential underlying conditions.

